  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "parseExtensions",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/IPv6Layer.cpp",
    "description": "IPv6Layer::parseExtensions() trusts the attacker-controlled IPv6 extension header length. Its loop verifies only that two bytes are available at the current offset, then constructs an extension and adds getExtensionLen() to offset/m_ExtensionsLen without checking that the complete extension fits in m_DataLen. This propagates an invalid IPv6 header length into parseNextLayer(); when the extension's nextHeader is GRE, the resulting payload pointer/length pair can refer beyond the captured packet, and GreLayer::getGREVersion() crashes while reading greData[1]. The GRE read is the crash site, while the missing extension-bound validation is the root cause.",
    "conditions": "A pcap/pcapng record must decode to an IPv6 packet containing a supported extension header (Hop-by-Hop, Destination, Routing, Fragment, or AH). The extension's length field must claim bytes inconsistent with the remaining captured IPv6 data, and the effective next-header value must select GRE. The fuzz harness writes the bytes as a capture file, PcapFileReaderDevice allocates only pkthdr.caplen bytes, Packet parses the IPv6 packet, and the unchecked extension length is carried into IPv6Layer::parseNextLayer(), which invokes GRE version detection on the invalid derived payload."
  },
